 Wilderness challenges
+
+Phase 6 — Agent Branch Push + PR Creation
+Goal: let the MammothOS agent carry an approved change from proposal to a reviewable pull request, without giving up human control at any gate.
+
+6.1 Scope
+Agent creates a new local branch per change; never commits to the selected checkout's current branch.
+
+Agent produces one commit per approved change with a descriptive message and the change ID.
+
+Agent pushes that branch to the remote under the mammoth/ namespace.
+
+Agent opens a pull request against the default branch with a summary, the diff, and validation evidence attached.
+
+6.2 Approval gates (all four required, in order)
+Gate 1 — Proposal: patch is reviewable; nothing is written to disk.
+
+Gate 2 — Validation run: explicit approval releases isolated Docker baseline-vs-candidate tests; no host execution.
+
+Gate 3 — Application: separate explicit approval commits the validated change to a new local branch. Never auto-merge.
+
+Gate 4 — Push + PR: separate explicit approval pushes the branch and opens the PR. Merge stays a human action in GitHub.
+
+6.3 Hard limits
+No automatic merge to main or any protected branch.
+
+No force-push, no branch-history rewrite, no deletion of remote branches.
+
+No deployment or production promotion triggered by the agent.
+
+Agent stops and reports once the PR is open; the next action is a human review.
+
+6.4 Evidence to attach to every PR
+Base SHA and resulting commit SHA.
+
+Validation profile used, with pass/fail summary for baseline and candidate.
+
+Explicit note that test profiles do not cover UI builds or CI workflow changes.
+
+Explicit statement of what was not verified.
 
